{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/994972-breaking-points-at-pilgrimage-1","id":994972,"title":"Breaking points at Pilgrimage 1","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-28T17:41:35-07:00","id":994972,"title":"Breaking points at Pilgrimage 1","content":"Question about the Pilgrimage breaking points and the table on page 178. If I'm at Pilgrimage 1 and I create a Pandoran or what have you, do I roll 5 dice as if I had Pilgrimage 2, or do I not roll at all? I ask because 179 says: &quot;[A Promethean] can never lose her last dot of Pilgrimage; if she otherwise would, she instead falls into Torment.&quot;<br /> <br /> One interpretation of that would be that you roll 5 dice, and if you fail you enter Torment instead of losing a dot. Is that right?<br /> <br /> Also, if you have Pilgrimage 3, do you roll 4 or 5 dice for a breaking point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu"